// The repos BESIDE the kit `spell` (checked out at `~/www/spell`):  projects of their own that use `spell` as any
// other project would (epic `repo-split` P20).
// - The kit's own folders -- `src/`, then `parser/`, `ui/`, `epic/` and `app/` -- are ONE repo and ONE package now:
//   they're its `package.json`'s `workspaces`, lowest first, not listed here.
// - None today:  spell-brand, the only one, was dropped (epic `epic-engine` T124).
// - Each repo here is its own git repo with its own install, at `path` from the kit's folder
//   (`../x` is `~/www/x`, beside `~/www/spell`):
//   - `name`:  its name on GitHub
//   - `url`:  where `yarn clone <name>` clones it from;  over SSH, falling back to HTTPS (GitHub's login, `gh auth`)
//   - `peer`:  a repo beside the kit the kit's tools know (epic-engine Q48):  the page server serves its part of the
//     settings (its `package.json`'s `"pageServer"`), from `path`;  a kit worktree has none beside it, so it uses
//     the main checkout's
// - Read by `tools/repos.ts` (`yarn clone`, `yarn pull`, `yarn status`, `yarn repos`), the page server's settings
//   (`peerRepos()`) and `spell rename imports`.
// - This file also marks a folder as a kit (`KIT_MARKER`).
{
  "repos": []
}
